  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1139 PM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nFriday morning, upper level troughing will start just east of us,\nand move into the southern Mississippi River Valley by Friday \nevening. Behind that trough, upper level ridging will push into \nthe area. We could see a few showers and thunderstorms in our \neastern counties on the west side of that trough, so have kept \nsome low (20%- 30%) chances for this. \n\nUpper level ridging will strengthen over the southern plains over\nthe weekend. This will keep our weather mainly dry, as well as \npush highs back up into the upper 90s to 105 degree range this \nweekend. Sunday night into Monday, an upper level low will move \ninto the Pacific Northwest, then into the northern plains. While \nthis system won't have any direct effect on our area, it will help\nto weaken the ridging in our area slightly, leading to slightly \ncooler temperatures from Monday through the second half of next \nweek. A cold frontal boundary is expected to move into the Texas \nPanhandle and Caprock region early next week which could result in\na low end chance for showers and thunderstorms for the northern \nhalf of the area.",
